{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Q2RgDeDcgM8VhrwviJzg7o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications accessible to implementers. This project derives specs from C source code, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies correctness through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go implementations), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `magefiles/` (build targets, scaffolded externally).\n\n**Implementation State** (trusting source_code over prose):\n- **Done** (code exists in source_code): `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`, `cmd/cat`, `cmd/sponge`, `cmd/du`, `cmd/wc`, `cmd/ls`, `cmd/true`, `cmd/false`, `cmd/version`\n- **Missing**: `cmd/true` has `main.go` but no `true_test.go` (contrast with `cmd/false` which has both). `cmd/yes`, `cmd/basename`, `cmd/dirname`, `cmd/tee`, `cmd/head`, `cmd/seq` have no code and specs are pending. `rel04.1` (ls-extended) is spec-complete but no code.\n\n**Current Release**: rel02.0 is the earliest incomplete release. Within it, `cmd/false` is complete (code + tests), `cmd/true` has code but no tests, and `yes`/`basename`/`dirname` have pending specs (human-authored, not a stitch target).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nThe earliest actionable gap is `cmd/true/true_test.go`. The implementation exists but has no differential tests — the only utility in the codebase with code but no test file. `cmd/false/false_test.go` provides the exact pattern to follow. This unblocks rel02.0 completion for the `true` utility.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/true differential tests for prd012-true R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.5\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd012-true.yaml (PRD for true utility)\n      - cmd/true/main.go (existing implementation to test)\n      - cmd/false/false_test.go (pattern for trivial utility differential tests)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (RunDiffTests API and DiffTest struct)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/true/true_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for true utility covering exit code, no output, and argument ignoring\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test prd012-true R1.1, R1.2, R1.3: true exits with code 0 and produces no output to stdout or stderr when invoked with no arguments\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test prd012-true R1.5: true silently ignores non-flag arguments (single arg, multiple args, unknown flags like --unknown) and still exits with code 0 with no output\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the cmd/false/false_test.go pattern exactly: TestMain builds the Go binary via go build and locates the GNU reference binary via exec.LookPath(\\\"gtrue\\\"); skip all tests if gtrue is not on PATH\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use testutils.RunDiffTests with DiffTest structs comparing Go binary against GNU gtrue from Homebrew coreutils; all tests set ExitCode: 0\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Mirror the two test functions from false_test.go: TestTrueNoArgs (R1.1, R1.2, R1.3) and TestTrueIgnoresArguments (R1.5) with three subtests -- single arg, multiple args, unknown flag\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/true/true_test.go compiles with no errors via go build ./cmd/true/...\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/true/... reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"TestTrueNoArgs verifies exit code 0 with no stdout and no stderr via RunDiffTests\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"TestTrueIgnoresArguments verifies single arg, multiple args, and unknown flag (--unknown) all exit 0 with no output via RunDiffTests\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"All test functions call t.Parallel() and follow the copyright header and package doc comment conventions from cmd/false/false_test.go\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":92646,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":92646},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"324a795b-57c7-4099-93cc-f0b689f6b66c","uuid":"0a5d432e-bc7c-4f3a-bb08-bd7d73dc1006"}
